WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:02.804
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:02.937 --> 00:05.855
See how curators grade evidence.

00:06.233 --> 00:09.826
How strong is the NDD evidence for an entity?

00:09.959 --> 00:16.297
An entity is a unique combination
of one gene, one mode of inheritance

00:16.430 --> 00:17.430
and one disease.

00:17.564 --> 00:21.549
To set its NDD evidence category,
curators count cases and families,

00:21.683 --> 00:25.471
combine criteria, and weigh the doubts.

00:25.833 --> 00:30.148
A Definitive entity needs at least one publication.

00:30.282 --> 00:33.892
Then count each individual and family once.

00:34.026 --> 00:37.189
Ten or more cases with <i>de novo</i> variants,

00:37.322 --> 00:42.587
five or more autosomal recessive
families with several affected individuals,

00:42.721 --> 00:45.838
or three or more families with X-chromosomal variants

00:45.972 --> 00:50.929
in several affected individuals:
each is a clear-cut frequency,

00:51.062 --> 00:54.703
and no further criteria are needed.

00:55.067 --> 01:00.840
For <i>ANKRD11</i> and KBG syndrome,
the synopsis reports <i>de novo</i>

01:00.973 --> 01:05.466
and some inherited variants
in more than 300 individuals.

01:05.599 --> 01:08.926
That is far more than ten <i>de novo</i> cases.

01:09.059 --> 01:11.785
This entity is Definitive.

01:12.167 --> 01:15.375
If the count falls short, combine.

01:15.509 --> 01:20.945
A strong frequency criterion,
such as three patients with <i>de novo</i> variants,

01:21.078 --> 01:26.744
needs a partner: one strong genetic criterion,
such as a recurrent variant;

01:26.877 --> 01:31.659
one strong clinical criterion,
such as a very specific phenotype;

01:31.792 --> 01:36.275
or at least two moderate criteria,
such as functional assays

01:36.408 --> 01:38.729
or missense constraint.

01:39.100 --> 01:42.910
The category belongs to the entity, not to the gene.

01:43.043 --> 01:46.340
<i>SETD1B</i> has two entities:
the autosomal dominant one is Definitive,

01:46.473 --> 01:52.433
the autosomal recessive one is Moderate.

01:52.800 --> 01:55.165
Open the recessive entity.

01:55.299 --> 01:59.085
Its synopsis reports bi-allelic missense variants

01:59.219 --> 02:04.244
in 3 independent individuals:
a strong frequency criterion.

02:04.377 --> 02:08.554
Without an additional genetic or
clinical criterion as a partner,

02:08.687 --> 02:14.594
it is Moderate: better than Limited,
but not enough for Definitive.

02:14.967 --> 02:18.523
<i>ZCCHC8</i> has one recessive family with a nonsense

02:18.656 --> 02:23.872
variant in three affected individuals.

02:24.005 --> 02:29.146
No further evidence is recorded,
so this entity is graded Limited.

02:29.533 --> 02:33.885
In borderline cases,
weigh the possible negative criteria.

02:34.019 --> 02:37.441
First, an old publication, never confirmed.

02:37.574 --> 02:40.481
Second, doubtful publication quality.

02:40.615 --> 02:44.442
Third, new evidence against the gene or its variants,

02:44.575 --> 02:50.365
such as constraint scores
from the Genome Aggregation Database, gnomAD.

02:50.499 --> 02:55.322
If the association is contradicted,
consider downgrading it to Limited,

02:55.456 --> 02:57.712
or even to Refuted.

02:58.100 --> 03:02.586
For <i>PGA5</i>, one individual was described in 2010,

03:02.719 --> 03:05.900
with no further publications since.

03:06.033 --> 03:11.841
In gnomAD, the gene is tolerant
to missense and loss-of-function variants.

03:11.974 --> 03:14.663
This entity is Refuted.

03:15.033 --> 03:18.373
The gene page shows the gnomAD scores.

03:18.506 --> 03:25.506
<i>PGA5</i> is not depleted for loss-of-function variants:
15.9 expected,

03:26.295 --> 03:27.295
18 observed.

03:27.433 --> 03:32.261
Remember to count each
individual and family once, per entity.

03:32.394 --> 03:36.123
A clear-cut frequency needs no further criteria.

03:36.256 --> 03:41.863
Otherwise, a strong frequency criterion
needs a genetic or clinical partner.

03:41.997 --> 03:45.535
In borderline cases, weigh the doubts.

03:45.900 --> 03:51.615
Find all the rules in the documentation
chapter Curation criteria.
